-		"details": "When your [CSP](https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/configuration#csp) enforces Trusted Types with `'require-trusted-types-for': ['script']`, Svelte creates HTML through a Trusted Types policy called `svelte-trusted-html`. Add it to the allowed policies:

```js
csp: {
	directives: {
		'require-trusted-types-for': ['script'],
		'trusted-types': ['svelte-trusted-html']
	}
}
```

This isn't needed if no page is rendered in the browser, i.e. every page has [`csr = false`](https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/page-options#csr)."

